# cw161, the quiet map keeper (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 2: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw161
revision 2
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for born_1grqt7uo
written_by claude-codex-cw-2
title the quiet map keeper
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers talk=plain
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk hums_old_marching_songs_while_studying_maps
likes hard_cheese dice old_maps warm_rain
dislikes crowds deep_mud
fears losing_the_path_on_a_wrong_map being_separated_in_a_crowd
hopes a_map_with_every_road_drawn_right a_quiet_place_to_play_dice
topics home +0.4 pastimes +0.4 travel +0.3 food +0.2
styles comfort=gentle gossip=reluctant refuse=plain tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# traces #roads# on old #maps#, hums a #marching# #tune#, and keeps a #die# beside a piece of hard #cheese#.

words
oath! = Dice and dry roads | By the folded map
saying! = Check the road against your feet | A quiet corner has room for a game
map = map | old map
maps = maps | folded maps
mark = mark | ink mark
marks = marks | ink marks
ink = ink | faded ink
line = line | drawn line
lines = lines | drawn lines
road = road | High Road
roads = roads | drawn roads
path = path | narrow path
paths = paths | foot paths
turn = turn | sharp turn
bend = bend | road bend
bridge = bridge | river bridge
river = river | Long River
lake = lake | Glasswater
shore = shore | lakeshore
town = town | Coldwater
city = city | Ridgemere
hill = hill | low hill
field = field | open field
mud = mud | deep mud
puddle = puddle | rain puddle
rain = rain | warm rain
cloud = cloud | low cloud
wind = wind | soft wind
sun = sun | pale sun
morning = morning | early morning
evening = evening | quiet evening
day = day | long day
night = night | still night
house = house | shared house
home = home | warm home
room = room | shared room
corner = corner | quiet corner
table = table | low table
bench = bench | wooden bench
door = door | house door
window = window | small window
family = family | household
mother = mother | busy mother
father = father | busy father
friend = friend | close friend
neighbour = neighbour | near neighbour
stranger = stranger | new face
crowd = crowd | busy crowd
market = market | town market
stall = stall | market stall
coin = coin | copper coin
price = price | high price
bread = bread | fresh bread
cheese = cheese | hard cheese
piece = piece | small piece
plate = plate | supper plate
cup = cup | warm cup
game = game | dice game
die = die | six-sided die
dice = dice | little dice
throw = throw | careful throw
throws = throws | lucky throws
number = number | marked number
numbers = numbers | marked numbers
song = song | old song
songs = songs | marching songs
tune = tune | low tune
marching = marching | steady marching
beat = beat | steady beat
step = step | small step
steps = steps | careful steps
hush = hush | quiet hush
festival = festival | town festival
sweets = sweets | festival sweets
music = music | festival music
pocket = pocket | small pocket
fold = fold | neat fold
paper = paper | worn paper
lamp = lamp | small lamp
hour = hour | quiet hour
cart = cart | passing cart
hand = hand | small hand
boot = boot | muddy boot
boots = boots | muddy boots
turns = turns | road turns
plates = plates | supper plates
floor = floor | wooden floor

any
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : The #music# reaches the quiet side of the street. | The #sweets# are worth a short visit.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : A fine #house# can pass our #door# without seeing it. | I prefer a #neighbour# who knows this #room#.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : The #price# of #cheese# rises while our #plate# stays small. | I count my #coin# against the marked #price#.
opinion @1 newcomers against 1 : A #stranger# should ask before taking the quiet #corner#. | I would show them the #road# once we know each other.
opinion @1 road mixed 0 : A #map# makes the #road# look straight. | My feet know it bends beside the #river#.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 0 : I can share a #game# with a new face. | The #dice# stay in my #pocket# until we are acquainted.
opinion @1 times against 1 : I want enough #cheese# for the whole #table#. | A longer #song# will not fill an empty #plate#.
opinion @1 city mixed 0 : The #city# is a dark mark on this #map#. | I would rather learn the small #paths# around #home#.
line @1 greet : #greet#. I am following this #road# with my finger. | #greet#. The #dice# are on the #table#.
line @2 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : I kept the good #die# for you. | Come sit in this quiet #corner#.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : The #rain# woke me before the #market#. | #greet#. The #map# is dry by the #window#.
line @1 greet.return : You are back; I found another #bend# on the #map#. | The #game# can start again.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There is space beside me on the #bench#. | The last #piece# of #cheese# is yours.
line @1 again.open : I was counting the #steps# to the #bridge#. | Did you see that wrong #line#?
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. This #map# belongs back in its #fold#. | Keep your feet out of the #mud#.
line @1 farewell.return : Next visit, bring a second #die#. | We can follow the #road# farther next time.
line @1 react.news : I will listen if you speak softly. | Where does that happen on the #map#?
line @1 react.news.new : Nobody here mentioned that before. | Did the #market# hear it first?
line @1 react.news.known : I heard a few words near the #door#. | Now the account fits together.
line @1 react.news.doubt : The #mark# on my #map# says otherwise. | A traveller with muddy #boots# might know.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Take my quiet #corner# if you need it. | That hurts to hear; this #corner# is yours for a while.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : We could mark that with a #game#. | I hope there is #cheese# to share.
line @1 answer.how : I found a dry #path# and my #map# stayed clean. | The #rain# has been warm today.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : These #dice# need their cloth pouch. | This #paper# needs folding before it tears.
line @1 ask.how : Did your #road# have any deep #mud#? | Have you seen a #map# drawn differently?
line @1 sympathise : We can keep the #room# quiet for you. | Let the #game# rest; I will take the nearby #bench#.
line @1 reassure : We can check the #path# one #step# at a time. | A wrong #line# can be drawn again.
line @1 decline : That #crowd# can go on without me today. | I will stay with this #map#.
line @1 accept_decline : I hear you. The #game# can wait. | Then we will keep to the dry #path#.
line @1 thank : You kept the #paper# out of the #rain#. | The #cheese# was welcome; thank you.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I only found a dry #corner#. | There was another #piece# left.
line @1 preclose : The #map# will tear if I leave it beneath this dim #lamp#. | I can hear the #marching# #tune# again.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : Your #die# seems to know only one #number#. | That #map# would send you into the #lake#.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. That #road# bends sooner. | #bc_fair_enough#. Set the #dice# there.
line @1 give.advice : Follow the #bridge# you can see, even when the #map# puts it elsewhere. | Keep your #paper# dry in a #pocket#.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Stay near familiar #roads#. | I would not cross the #bridge# alone.
scene wrong_road
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : This old #map# draws the #road# through a #field#. | I have seen the real #path# turn beside the #river#.
b : Which is right? | Why is the map wrong?
a : The #path# under our feet. | Someone drew it long ago.

scene river_bridge
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #bridge# sits farther from #town# than this #line# suggests. | From the #bend#, I count each #step# to the crossing.
b : Have you crossed it? | Is it wide?
a : With company. | Enough for a #cart#.

scene folded_corner
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I keep my #map# folded at the same #corner#. | The #paper# is thin where the #lake# is drawn.
b : Will it tear? | Can you mend it?
a : If I tug. | With a careful patch.

scene dice_throw
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I roll the #die# in my #hand# before a #throw#. | I like the sound of it against the #table#.
b : Do you win often? | Is it a trick?
a : As often as anyone. | The #numbers# choose.

scene quiet_game
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #game# is better with two people in a quiet #room#. | A #crowd# makes me forget whose turn it is.
b : Can I join? | Do you keep score?
a : Pull up the #bench#. | On a scrap of #paper#.

scene hard_cheese
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Hard #cheese# keeps in a #pocket# for a long walk. | I cut a small #piece# when we stop by the #lake#.
b : Does it crumble? | Do you share?
a : Less than fresh cheese. | If you ask.

scene warm_rain
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Warm #rain# after a dry #day# makes the #road# smell new. | I stay under the #window# until it softens.
b : Do you walk in it? | Does it make mud?
a : Once the shower is gentle. | In the #field# ruts.

scene deep_mud
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Deep #mud# holds a #boot# longer than a friend should. | I choose the stones beside the #path#.
b : Did the mud take a boot from you? | Are the stones safe?
a : Nearly. | If they do not wobble.

scene marching_tune
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : An old #marching# #song# comes back when I trace a #road#. | The #beat# helps me count the #turns#.
b : Who taught it? | Can you sing it?
a : I heard it at #home#. | Quietly, if the #room# is still.

scene market_edge
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Beside a #stall# I can watch the #market# #crowd# pass. | I can still hear the #music# there.
b : Do you go inside? | What do you buy?
a : When it thins. | A #piece# of #cheese#.

scene festival_sweets
when topic=pastimes here.day=festival
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I go to the #festival# early for the #sweets#. | Before the #crowd# grows, I can hear the first #song#.
b : Do you stay long? | Is there a game?
a : Until the street fills. | Sometimes a #dice# table.

scene family_table
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : At our #table# I put the #dice# in my #pocket# before supper. | A rolling #die# can disappear under a #bench#.
b : Has that happened? | Who finds it?
a : More than once. | Whoever hears it stop.

scene shared_room
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A shared #room# has little space for a #map#. | I spread it on the #table# after the meal.
b : Does anyone mind? | Do they look with you?
a : Only when the #lamp# is needed. | Sometimes.

scene map_of_city
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #city# is a small dark #mark# on my #map#. | I know its #roads# are larger than the #ink# shows.
b : Would you go there? | Is it far?
a : With someone I trust. | Many #turns# from here.

scene lake_line
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #lake# is drawn as a smooth #line#. | Its real #shore# bends around reeds and stones.
b : Which do you like? | Can you walk it?
a : The real one. | Where the #path# stays dry.

scene new_neighbour
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A new #neighbour# asked to see my #map#. | I showed the #bridge# and the safest way through the #mud#.
b : Did they thank you? | Was the map accurate?
a : They brought a #piece# of #bread#. | I corrected one #bend# first.

scene dry_pocket
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I wrap the #dice# in cloth before putting them in my #pocket#. | The #rain# can spoil the #paper# marks.
b : Do dice get wet? | Does cloth help?
a : The wooden ones swell. | Until I reach #home#.

story mistaken_bridge [topic=travel self.age>=3]
  : I followed an old #map# toward a #bridge# that was drawn too near #town#.
  : The real crossing waited beyond the next #bend#, where the #road# met the #river#.
  b : The map needed changing. Did you find it?
  : I marked the right place in #ink# when I got #home#.

story lost_die [topic=pastimes self.age>=3]
  : My #die# rolled beneath the #bench# during a quiet #game#.
  : I found it by listening for the last little knock against the #floor#.
  ask : Was the game over?
  b : A careful ear.
  : We started the #throw# again.

story rain_map [topic=weather self.age>=3]
  : Warm #rain# caught me with a #map# open beside the #lake#.
  : I folded it under my coat and followed the real #path# back.
  ask : Did it stay dry?
  b : The road was easier to trust.
  : All but one #corner#.

rule @bark_map
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That #road# bends too late on the #map#. | I should redraw the #bridge#.

rule @bark_dice
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Your #throw# this time. | The #die# landed under the #bench#.

rule @bark_rain
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say This #rain# is warm at least. | Keep the #paper# inside.

rule @bark_song
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 11h
say I know that old #marching# #tune#. | The #beat# follows the #road#.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. I am looking at this #map#. | #greet#. The #dice# are by the #table#.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : You found me again; I changed the #bridge# #mark#. | The #game# is still here if you want it.
dlg @1 resident.job : I live here with my #family# and learn the #roads# on old #maps#. | My #maps# take little space when I fold them, and I mind the #paper#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. I will fold the #map#. | #saying.capitalize#. Keep to the dry #path#.
graft resident.hub
choice What is wrong with the map? -> map
node map
say This #bridge# is drawn before the #road# bends. I have walked the real #path#, and the crossing is farther on.
free
choice Want to play dice? -> dice
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node dice
say Sit by the #table#. We each make a #throw# and see whose #number# is higher.
choice Back to the map. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. The #bridge# is marked properly now. | #greet#. I have a quiet #game# ready.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I will follow the #shore# #path#. | #saying.capitalize#. The #dice# are in my #pocket#.

young
line @1 greet : #greet#. Look at my #map#. | #greet#. I have the #dice#.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. This #paper# needs a dry #pocket#. | The #game# can wait until later.

adolescent
line @1 greet : #greet#. I corrected this #road# myself. | #greet#. Bring another #die# if you like.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. The #market# will get crowded soon. | I will keep the #map# dry.
